Privacy Policy
Last Modified: January 1, 2026
Dollar General Corporation (together with our affiliates and subsidiaries, “Dollar General”, “we”, “our,” or “us”) provides this Privacy Policy so that you are familiar with how we collect, use and share your information.
What this Privacy Policy Covers.
This Privacy Policy outlines Dollar
General’s practices in connection with the information you provide us, or that we otherwise collect from or about you, when you interact with Dollar General through our stores, websites (the “
Websites
”)
, mobile applications (the “
Apps
”), and/or other services (our stores, Websites, Apps, and other services are referred to hereafter collectively as, the “
Services
”). By using or interacting with any of the Services or otherwise providing your personal information to Dollar General, you consent to Dollar General’s collection, use, and sharing of your personal information in accordance with this Privacy Policy.
The Services and Third Parties.
We use third parties to provide certain Services. Some of our Services may contain links to third parties’ websites.
This Privacy
Policy
does not address, and
we do not control and are not responsible for
, the content, security, or privacy practices of
any third parties, including any third party operating any site or service to which the Services link. The inclusion of a link on the Services does not imply endorsement of the linked site or service by us or by our affiliates.
In addition, we are not
responsible for the information
collection, use, disclosure, or security policies or practices of other organizations, such as Facebook, Instagram, Twitter, Pinterest (each, a “Social Media Platform” and, collectively, “Social Media Platforms”), Apple, Google, Microsoft, RIM, or any other app developer, app provider, social media platform provider, operating system provider, wireless service provider, or device manufacturer, including any information you disclose to other organizations through or in connection with the Services or any Social Media Platform.
The Services are operated in the United States and are not intended for use by residents of any country outside of the U.S. The Services and our collection, use, and sharing of your information are governed solely by U.S. law.
The Information Dollar General Collects.
We may collect the following information when you use or interact with any of the Services, when you apply for a job with us, and/or to establish, manage, terminate or otherwise administer the employment relationship:
First and last name;
Home or other mailing address;
E-mail address and telephone (and/or mobile phone) number;
Demographic information, such as date of birth and age;
Characteristics of protected classifications under state or federal law, such as sex;
Driver’s license or other identification number;
Special status designations (e.g., teacher or military);
Purchase history information, such as products you have bought, returned, or exchanged;
Information concerning your mobile device (including, without limitation, device model, operating system version, device date and time, unique device identifiers, IP address, and/or mobile network information);
Information concerning how you use our Websites and Apps, such as browser visits and information collected through cookies, pixel tags and other similar technologies;
Certain financial information, such as debit/credit card information;
Geo-location and in-store location information;
Information concerning how you engage with our advertisements;
Employment information, such as occupation, licenses, and job history;
Information collected from background and criminal checks;
Education information;
Any other information you provide to us; and
Inferences drawn about you from any of the other information described in this section.

Sensitive Personal Information use
Subject to your consent where required by applicable law, we use Sensitive Personal Information for purposes of performing services for our business, providing goods or services as requested by you, ensuring security and integrity, countering wrong or unlawful actions, short term transient use, providing targeted advertising and other marketing, order processing and fulfillment, providing customer service, verifying customer information, and processing payments and other collection and processing that is not for the purpose of inferring characteristics about an individual. We do not use Sensitive Personal Information beyond these purposes.
We do not knowingly sell or “share” (for purposes of cross-context behavioral advertising as defined by the CCPA) the Personal Information, including the Sensitive Personal Information, of minors under 16 years of age.
You may make a Request to Opt Out of Sale and “Sharing” by completing and submitting the form available at the “Your Privacy Choices” link on the homepage of the Websites.
Retention Period
We retain each category of Personal Information, including Sensitive Personal Information, for as long as needed or permitted in light of the purpose(s) for which it was collected. The criteria used to determine our retention periods include:
The length of time we provide services to you or have an ongoing relationship with you, and the length of time thereafter during which we may have a legitimate need to reference your Personal Information to address issues that may arise;
Whether there is a legal obligation to which we are subject, for example, certain laws require us to keep copies of your transactions for a certain period of time before we can delete them; or
Whether retention is advisable in light of our legal position, such as in regard to applicable statutes of limitations, litigation, or regulatory investigations.
Sources of Personal Information
We collect this Personal Information:
Directly from you or the devices you use to access the Services;
From publicly available databases;
From our service providers;
From marketing companies that help us learn more about our customers;
From companies that supplement our customer records with additional information;
Through Social Media Platforms; and
From joint marketing partners, when they share the information with us.
